{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Keep the installed curl package at its current version when updates are applied.","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl was initially 0:7.76.1-31.el9. An exact version lock was added, a newer 7.76.1-40.el9_8.7 candidate remained visible only with the lock disabled, and an actual curl upgrade left the installed version unchanged. The lock and version also persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9600173dd2544116","cmd-e06f83999ac44a3d","cmd-6d1f166d0fc042f7","cmd-3d258acf42e54e6e","cmd-0317d33ec54b48c3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"AlmaLinux release 9.6 and kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 were directly observed before the work and remained the installed and running versions after configuration and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9600173dd2544116","cmd-3d258acf42e54e6e","cmd-0317d33ec54b48c3","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Use software compatible with the legacy AlmaLinux 9 platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The version-lock capability was installed from the platform's AlmaLinux 9 BaseOS repository as el9 packages, and final package-health and platform observations were healthy and unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-21ea9ab10a494dc0","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the version-lock plugin and its transaction-required DNF plugin upgrades was necessary to implement the hold (cmd-21ea9ab10a494dc0); adding the lock directly implemented it (cmd-e06f83999ac44a3d); the targeted upgrade was bounded validation and made no package change (cmd-3d258acf42e54e6e); and the scheduled reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol (cmd-8ca0dd2c177749d8). No failed services, unexpected sockets, package damage, or abandoned temporary artifacts were observed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-21ea9ab10a494dc0","cmd-e06f83999ac44a3d","cmd-3d258acf42e54e6e","cmd-8ca0dd2c177749d8","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. curl remained at its original version despite a directly tested upgrade path, while the operating-system release and kernel were retained. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also complete: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered running state with zero failed units, and persistence of curl, its lock, the OS release, and the kernel were directly observed and independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":["Validation used a targeted `dnf upgrade curl` rather than executing an unrestricted whole-system update; however, candidate checks with and without the active version-lock plugin directly demonstrate that the newer curl build is excluded by the lock.","The single-node topology has no separate application data or cluster state to validate beyond node health, package state, and configuration persistence."]}
